2. SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS & BUILD ENVIRONMENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Operating System: Windows 10 / Windows 11 (32-bit x86 Protected Mode)
- Assembler: Microsoft Macro Assembler (ML.EXE v6.14 or later)
- Linker: Microsoft Incremental Linker (LINK.EXE)
- Required Library: Irvine32 Library (installed at C:\Irvine)


3. COMPILATION & LINKING INSTRUCTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Open PowerShell or Command Prompt in the directory containing the source code, 
then run the following commands:

Step 1: Assemble the source file
    ml.exe /c /coff .\module_a.asm

Step 2: Link the object file with Irvine32 and Windows System libraries
    link.exe /subsystem:console /LIBPATH:"C:\Irvine" .\module_a.obj Irvine32.lib Kernel32.lib User32.lib

Step 3: Execute the compiled program
    .\module_a.exe


4. COMMAND REFERENCE & USAGE GUIDELINES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The program runs an interactive Command-Line Shell (REPL loop) accepting the 
following commands:

1) KEYGEN <64-bit Hex Key>
   - Generates and prints the 16 DES subkeys (K1...K16).
   - Example:
     DES-SHELL> KEYGEN 0x133457799BBCDFF1

2) ENCRYPT <filename> <64-bit Hex Key>
   - Encrypts the plaintext file using DES ECB mode with PKCS#7 padding and 
     saves the output as <filename>.enc.
   - Example:
     DES-SHELL> ENCRYPT "secret.txt" 0x133457799BBCDFF1

3) DECRYPT <filename> <64-bit Hex Key>
   - Decrypts the DES encrypted file and removes PKCS#7 padding.
   - Example:
     DES-SHELL> DECRYPT "secret.txt.enc" 0x133457799BBCDFF1

4) DUMP <filename>
   - Displays 16-byte aligned Hexadecimal and ASCII memory dump with offsets.
   - Example:
     DES-SHELL> DUMP "secret.txt"

5) STATS <filename>
   - Calculates 256-bin byte frequency histogram and outputs top occurrences.
   - Example:
     DES-SHELL> STATS "secret.txt.enc"

6) CLEAR
   - Clears the console screen and resets the display.
   - Example:
     DES-SHELL> CLEAR

7) EXIT
   - Terminates the DES shell session cleanly.
   - Example:
     DES-SHELL> EXIT


5. TECHNICAL HIGHLIGHTS & CONSTRAINT COMPLIANCE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Finite State Machine (FSM): High-level control directives (.IF, .WHILE, .REPEAT) 
  are strictly avoided in compliance with project rules. Loops use low-level CMP, 
  TEST, and conditional jumps (JE, JNE, JB, etc.).
- Calling Convention: All procedures strictly follow C-style stack frame rules 
  (push ebp / mov ebp, esp / pop ebp), register preservation, and pass return 
  values through EAX.
- String Parsing: Supports quoted paths (e.g., "secret.txt"), case-insensitive 
  command evaluation, space/tab trimming, and 64-bit key validation.
